WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:06.090
The Merc with a Mouth may be in for a Marvel-sized
reality check if or, more realistically, when

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:07.500
he joins the MCU.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.760
After enjoying two refreshingly batty films
with Deadpool 1 &amp; 2, audiences worldwide have

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.160
been wondering what's coming next.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:18.900
Fans of the no-holds-barred superhero franchise
were initially over the moon when star Ryan

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.460
Reynolds recently announced that the potty-mouthed
hero would soon be making his MCU debut.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.780
With the tentatively titled Deadpool 3 now
officially in production under the Marvel

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:33.040
Studios shingle by way of its parent company
Disney it seems MCU mastermind Kevin Feige

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:36.120
could be eyeing major changes for the Deadpool
franchise.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:41.620
The latest little nugget of MCU rumor madness
comes via the not-super-reliable rumor-mongers

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:47.210
over at We Got This Covered, who are reporting
an alleged emphasis on "alleged" Marvel insider's

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:51.760
claims that Feige is looking to replace some
key creatives behind the Deadpool franchise.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.420
Don't worry, he's apparently not looking to
push Ryan Reynolds out of the picture and

00:00:55.420 --> 00:01:01.150
recast the role of Wade Wilson but according
to WGTC, Feige is looking to take some creative

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:02.840
control out of Reynolds' hands.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.740
As a reminder, Reynolds has served as producer
and a key creative force behind both Deadpool

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:12.210
and Deadpool 2, hand-picking director David
Leitch for the sequel and even earning a writing

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.620
credit for his work on that film.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:18.060
It's been speculated that Reynolds was pushing
to bring the creative team behind Deadpool

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:22.640
2 back for the upcoming sequel, including
his co-writers Rhett Reese and Paul Wernick.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:27.080
Feige, according to the rumor, isn't sold
on bringing Leitch back to helm Deadpool 3

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:31.140
and is reportedly keen on bringing Ant-Man
and the Wasp scribes Chris Mckenna and Eric

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.480
Sommers on board to fully Marvel-ize the sequel.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.140
Way to pull the rug out from under these folks,
Marvel!

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.100
"Hah!

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.380
Fake laugh… hiding real pain."

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.530
As for what those supposed changes could mean
for Deadpool 3, it's possible that the Merc

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:49.320
we've come to know and love over the course
of the first two deliriously crass Deadpool

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.040
movies may be toned way, way down.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.600
Of course, that may not be entirely a bad
thing.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.619
While the first two Deadpool movies have served
as a welcome departure from the increasingly

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:03.120
homogenized realm of superhero cinema, even
the characters' most ardent fans would likely

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.320
admit the winking meta schtick was wearing
a little thin by the end of Deadpool 2.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:12.180
Still, that wickedly self-aware approach has
spawned a hyper-specific style in the movies,

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:16.500
and it's sort of impossible to imagine what
Deadpool 3 might look like without it.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.320
"You might wanna look away for this.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.360
Now, this little piggy went to — "

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:26.739
Deadpool remains a singular voice in the Marvel
canon, so much so that a stark change in tone

00:02:26.739 --> 00:02:31.469
might leave his new flick all but unrecognizable
from its cinematic brethren, not to mention

00:02:31.469 --> 00:02:32.160
the comics.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:36.200
To date, the decision by Reynolds and the
Deadpool creatives to lean headlong into the

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:40.469
comics' special brand of wacky is a big part
of what has set the franchise apart from every

00:02:40.469 --> 00:02:41.980
other superhero story out there.

00:02:42.329 --> 00:02:46.660
If Team Marvel is indeed looking to shake
things up, the changes might be to the detriment

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:47.620
of Deadpool 3.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:53.200
However, as we previously mentioned, WGTC's
report is in no way confirmed, and it may

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.669
in fact all be a bunch of hot air let's face
it: WGTC isn't exactly known for their pinpoint

00:02:58.669 --> 00:02:59.300
accuracy.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:03.960
Plus, Feige is a pretty smart guy, and changing
or eliminating everything that makes the Deadpool

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.960
franchise unique doesn't exactly sound like
his style.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.020
Regardless of whether a change in direction
is in the cards, it does appear that a good

00:03:11.029 --> 00:03:15.630
deal of the previous flicks' cast may be back
for Deadpool 3 though some fan faves might

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:16.220
not be.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:21.180
TJ Miller, who appeared as Wilson's buddy
Weasel in the first two films, and Brianna

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:25.189
Hildebrand, who portrayed the wonderfully
surly Negasonic Teenage Warhead, are both

00:03:25.189 --> 00:03:26.280
still on the fence.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:30.940
WGTC has reported that Hildebrand may not
return but, again, their reports should be

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:35.600
taken with a grain of salt and according to
CBR, Miller is iffy on the prospect of reprising

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.700
his role, though he is under contract.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:41.659
"Just once, I'm gonna find a planet of people
that are worse than me at everything.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:43.560
A whole bunch of functional idiots.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.980
I'm gonna go there, and I'm gonna be their
Superman."

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:47.060
"...Isn't that Canada?"

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:51.780
Marvel is apparently eager to bring two of
Deadpool 2's standouts back for the new film,

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:56.140
however: ScreenRant reports that Zazie Beetz
has a three-picture deal and is set to return

00:03:56.150 --> 00:04:00.010
as Domino, and Josh Brolin has a similar deal
that should ensure that he'll reprise the

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:03.480
role of Cable at least another time or two
according to SlashFilm.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:07.799
With those heavy hitters seemingly on board
for Deadpool 3, it seems even more likely

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:12.360
Kevin Feige and Marvel will stay the course,
weaving the R-rated, jaw-droppingly vulgar

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.340
Wade Wilson we all know and love into the
MCU fabric.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:20.100
This is our sincere hope because without his
potty mouth, is Deadpool even Deadpool at

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:20.600
all?

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:21.760
We think not.

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:25.760
We'll be filling you in on all the Deadpool
3 news that's fit to report as soon as it

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:26.580
becomes available.

